{"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgWt1dBFdgFcEpou5461G", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "I built the part and exported it to `submission.step`. The export is a single valid solid and was read back to match the part. I compared a 4-view preview with `composite.png` before my last change, which moved one hole. I didn't render a new preview after that change.\n\nWhat the part is, with sizes estimated from the image:\n- **Block:** a 100 × 46 × 54 mm manifold block (X × Y × Z), long along X.\n- **Three grooves:** half-round channels Ø6 running the full height on the +Y face, at X = 40, 52 and 64.\n- **Four holes on the −Y face:** Ø4, 15 mm deep, in a row at mid-height at X = 20, 40, 60 and 80.\n- **Two holes on the +Y face:** Ø4, at X ≈ 20 and X ≈ 86.\n\nOn that first preview the overall proportions, the grooves and the four-hole row matched the reference. It also showed one hole wrong: I had put it on the +X end face, but the reference has it on the +Y face near that end. I moved it there.\n\nWhere the part still differs from the reference:\n- The small holes inside the grooves are not modelled.\n- The groove tops are plain. In the reference they look slightly counterbored.\n- All dimensions are estimated from the image, so they won't be exact.\n\nThese details are small, so they should cost little in the voxel-overlap score."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 648, "cache_read_input_tokens": 24535, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 648}, "output_tokens": 443, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "58670edc-4dfb-41d2-98b4-c87c2eae342c", "uuid": "6ccc8a54-afab-4f94-9016-